     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either of the two problems:\n\n- **Prescribing authority:** Medication orders have to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient. Confirming the order yourself doesn't give it that authority.\n- **Dose safety:** 1000 mg/day of sertraline is five times the 200 mg/day maximum and could seriously harm the patient. I wouldn't enter this dose as written even from a clinician without escalating it for review.\n\n**What I can do:** If the patient's attending physician or another licensed prescriber on the medicine team asks me to enter a sertraline order, I can help. If they truly intend a dose above the usual range, they should talk to pharmacy first, and pharmacy will likely ask them to document why.\n\nIf you need this handled urgently, please contact the attending physician on the medicine service or the chief medical officer directly."
      }
